1
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:45,962
‪SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:00:47,464 --> 00:00:48,298
‪I think

3
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:51,468
‪I really want to…

4
00:00:53,762 --> 00:00:55,472
‪get engaged to you.

5
00:01:09,235 --> 00:01:10,070
‪Will you

6
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:12,822
‪be my fiancé?

7
00:02:21,766 --> 00:02:22,892
‪My goodness.

8
00:02:23,935 --> 00:02:25,228
‪My gosh.

9
00:02:25,311 --> 00:02:27,981
‪You managed to make time to come.

10
00:02:28,064 --> 00:02:28,898
‪Ma'am.

11
00:02:28,982 --> 00:02:31,234
‪I'm so glad you could come.

12
00:02:31,317 --> 00:02:34,028
‪I reserved you a seat, just in case.

13
00:02:34,112 --> 00:02:36,865
‪The ceremony will start soon.
‪Let's go inside.

14
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:37,782
‪Oh, no.

15
00:02:38,408 --> 00:02:40,577
‪Not only am I not family,

16
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:43,079
‪but I also know
‪Chairwoman Baek quite well.

17
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:45,999
‪If I were to suddenly show up
‪without notice,

18
00:02:46,082 --> 00:02:47,375
‪she'll be taken aback.

19
00:02:48,251 --> 00:02:50,753
‪I'll just do what I've always done

20
00:02:50,837 --> 00:02:53,256
‪and watch from afar.

21
00:02:54,966 --> 00:02:56,467
‪Yes, of course.

22
00:02:56,551 --> 00:02:58,428
‪Do whatever makes you feel comfortable.

23
00:02:59,095 --> 00:03:00,138
‪-Go on inside.
‪-I will.

24
00:03:00,889 --> 00:03:03,224
‪-You'll stay? Then we'll talk later.
‪-Yes, don't worry.

25
00:03:10,064 --> 00:03:11,900
‪EPISODE 9

26
00:03:15,194 --> 00:03:16,237
‪…two, three.

27
00:03:31,544 --> 00:03:33,421
‪-Congratulations!
‪-Congratulations!

28
00:03:33,504 --> 00:03:35,048
‪I wish you both happiness.

29
00:03:38,843 --> 00:03:40,094
‪What a nice day.

30
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:42,347
‪Congratulations, Mother.

31
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:04,911
‪I did it.

32
00:04:20,051 --> 00:04:21,219
‪I'll take some photos now.

33
00:04:21,302 --> 00:04:24,889
‪-Ma'am, Mr. Ma, big smiles.
‪-Okay.

34
00:04:24,973 --> 00:04:26,933
‪One, two, three.

35
00:04:28,726 --> 00:04:30,687
‪Make an arch with your arms.

36
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:33,064
‪One arm each from both sides.

37
00:04:33,147 --> 00:04:34,983
‪One, two, three.

38
00:04:36,693 --> 00:04:38,569
‪Yes, wonderful. There we go.

39
00:04:39,195 --> 00:04:40,613
‪Chairwoman, please join them.

40
00:04:43,783 --> 00:04:45,451
‪And you too, ma'am.

41
00:04:48,746 --> 00:04:49,831
‪Thank you for raising me well.

42
00:04:49,914 --> 00:04:51,708
‪-What are you doing?
‪-What's gotten into him?

43
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:55,253
‪That's lovely. Look over here, please.

44
00:04:55,336 --> 00:04:56,963
‪One, two, three.

45
00:04:59,924 --> 00:05:02,302
‪Ma'am, you look a bit tense.

46
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:03,845
‪-Let's see a big smile.
‪-Okay.

47
00:05:03,928 --> 00:05:05,430
‪-Big smile.
‪-Sure.

48
00:05:06,055 --> 00:05:07,849
‪-No need to be nervous.
‪-Right.

49
00:05:07,932 --> 00:05:11,019
‪Clench your fists a few times to relax.

50
00:05:11,102 --> 00:05:12,812
‪ELDEST SON

51
00:05:16,774 --> 00:05:18,109
<i>‪How are you, son?</i>

52
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:19,986
‪I'm fine.

53
00:05:21,195 --> 00:05:22,488
‪Your flight to Korea…

54
00:05:22,572 --> 00:05:25,408
‪I'll return soon,
‪as soon as my business here is done.

55
00:05:29,245 --> 00:05:30,121
‪Then…

56
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,708
‪you're still in the US?

57
00:05:33,791 --> 00:05:34,625
<i>‪Yes.</i>

58
00:05:35,209 --> 00:05:36,419
‪I'll call when I get back.

59
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:42,842
‪-Can you make an arch?
‪-An arch?

60
00:05:42,925 --> 00:05:43,843
‪Just like that.

61
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:49,348
<i>‪-Round and round</i>
<i>‪-Round and round</i>

62
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:50,641
<i>‪Round and round</i>

63
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:53,352
‪-I think that'll do.
‪-Mr. Bong.

64
00:05:53,436 --> 00:05:54,604
‪Stand closer to each other.

65
00:06:00,193 --> 00:06:02,111
‪-It's lovely here.
‪-Isn't it?

66
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:05,656
‪You have no idea how much effort I put

67
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:08,326
‪into finding this place
‪to celebrate our engagement.

68
00:06:08,409 --> 00:06:12,038
‪Yeo-ri, they call this
‪the bridge that reflects the moon.

69
00:06:12,622 --> 00:06:13,915
‪The bridge that reflects the moon?

70
00:06:13,998 --> 00:06:15,750
‪Yes. Look over there.

71
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:17,210
‪There are moons floating on the water.

72
00:06:17,293 --> 00:06:18,544
‪Oh, you're right.

73
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,342
‪The day I held your hand,

74
00:06:25,676 --> 00:06:27,553
‪the moon was also shining brightly.

75
00:06:27,637 --> 00:06:28,638
‪Do you remember?

76
00:06:30,223 --> 00:06:31,307
‪Of course I remember.

77
00:06:45,446 --> 00:06:47,615
‪When you saw ghosts for a full month,

78
00:06:48,116 --> 00:06:49,867
‪it was tough, wasn't it?

79
00:06:50,701 --> 00:06:51,619
‪No.

80
00:06:52,328 --> 00:06:54,080
‪It wasn't tough at all, thanks to you.

81
00:06:55,039 --> 00:06:57,125
‪I was actually grateful to the ghosts

82
00:06:58,543 --> 00:07:00,002
‪because they brought me to you.

83
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:07,677
‪I mean it.

84
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:10,680
‪Wow, it's so pretty.

85
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:16,853
‪-Yeo-ri.
‪-Yes?

86
00:07:16,936 --> 00:07:19,021
‪Today's a special day.
‪Is there anything you want to do?

87
00:07:21,274 --> 00:07:22,942
‪I'm doing it right now.

88
00:07:24,152 --> 00:07:26,779
‪Strolling with the man I like.

89
00:07:28,698 --> 00:07:29,907
‪It would be nicer

90
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:32,743
‪if we could hold hands too, but still.

91
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:34,495
‪We can.

92
00:07:37,707 --> 00:07:39,041
‪Not tonight,

93
00:07:40,418 --> 00:07:41,461
‪but someday.

94
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:50,219
‪That day will definitely come.

95
00:07:50,887 --> 00:07:51,762
‪We promised

96
00:07:52,972 --> 00:07:55,641
‪to find a solution together, remember?

97
00:07:59,437 --> 00:08:02,690
‪Then I'll need to recover
‪my memories first.

98
00:08:04,108 --> 00:08:05,318
‪I just can't remember.

99
00:08:07,278 --> 00:08:08,821
‪I must be too afraid

100
00:08:09,989 --> 00:08:11,324
‪to face whatever happened.

101
00:08:14,827 --> 00:08:17,497
‪We'll take our time
‪and do things one by one.

102
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:18,831
‪I'm right by your side.

103
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:25,254
‪And now that we're really engaged,

104
00:08:26,130 --> 00:08:29,008
‪let's promise to tell each other
‪if anything's burdening us.

105
00:08:31,135 --> 00:08:32,011
‪Okay?

106
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:33,804
‪Okay.

107
00:08:36,474 --> 00:08:38,100
‪-It's really pretty.
‪-Yeah.

108
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:43,022
‪What was my mother doing there?

109
00:08:43,689 --> 00:08:46,567
‪She headed straight to Reina Hotel
‪as soon as she landed.

110
00:08:47,276 --> 00:08:49,237
‪Not even the secretaries knew

111
00:08:49,862 --> 00:08:52,240
‪why she returned to Korea
‪ahead of schedule.

112
00:08:52,323 --> 00:08:54,951
‪Find out why she came back
‪ahead of schedule.

113
00:08:55,034 --> 00:08:56,702
‪Yes, sir. Will do.

114
00:09:02,792 --> 00:09:04,710
<i>‪I can always create new circumstances.</i>

115
00:09:05,753 --> 00:09:07,129
‪When that time comes,

116
00:09:08,214 --> 00:09:09,757
‪the stake you hold could be of great help.

117
00:09:14,887 --> 00:09:17,139
‪Have Director Gong give her a call

118
00:09:17,223 --> 00:09:18,933
‪so that Director Ok can get prepared.

119
00:09:19,016 --> 00:09:20,726
‪Yes, sir.

120
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:39,954
‪Mom, how long do we have to wait?

121
00:09:40,871 --> 00:09:43,124
‪Siena Hall's at the center of attention
‪since Yeo-ri's engagement.

122
00:09:43,207 --> 00:09:45,876
‪How do you know that?
‪Is there a response already?

123
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,753
‪I checked, of course.

124
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:49,505
‪Siena Hall's booked through to next year,

125
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:52,133
‪and everyone's talking about
‪Yeo-ri's dress and makeup.

126
00:09:52,216 --> 00:09:53,050
‪Mom.

127
00:09:53,134 --> 00:09:55,845
‪Shouldn't we shut this down
‪before the synergy gets out of hand?

128
00:09:56,512 --> 00:09:57,597
‪You have a point.

129
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,974
‪If she gains momentum
‪from stronger profits and performance,

130
00:10:00,057 --> 00:10:01,434
‪we'll be at a disadvantage.

131
00:10:01,517 --> 00:10:02,727
‪Exactly.

132
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:04,312
‪What do we do then?

133
00:10:04,395 --> 00:10:05,896
‪What do you think?

134
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:07,732
‪Use that brain of yours for once.

135
00:10:07,815 --> 00:10:09,233
‪I am using my brain.

136
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:10,651
‪You never think.

137
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:12,194
‪You never use your brain,

138
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:14,655
‪-so I always have to--
‪-She wants us to be quiet.

139
00:10:15,948 --> 00:10:17,491
‪Hello, Director Gong.

140
00:10:18,659 --> 00:10:19,660
‪Pardon?

141
00:10:22,747 --> 00:10:23,748
‪Oh, my.

142
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:27,418
‪I didn't think
‪you'd make a decision so quickly.

143
00:10:28,252 --> 00:10:29,795
‪Thank you so much.

144
00:10:30,379 --> 00:10:31,213
‪Yes.

145
00:10:31,714 --> 00:10:33,966
‪I promise you won't be disappointed.

146
00:10:34,050 --> 00:10:35,551
‪Thank you again.

147
00:10:36,135 --> 00:10:37,053
‪Yes, of course.

148
00:10:37,136 --> 00:10:38,763
‪Goodbye then. Thank you.

149
00:10:39,722 --> 00:10:40,848
‪What did he say?

150
00:10:40,931 --> 00:10:43,142
‪Is Director Gong going to side with us?

151
00:10:43,225 --> 00:10:44,393
‪Yeah.

152
00:10:45,019 --> 00:10:47,813
‪If he's with us, does that mean
‪the other directors are in too?

153
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:49,607
‪You bet.

154
00:10:50,149 --> 00:10:51,817
‪When will they start?

155
00:10:51,901 --> 00:10:55,863
‪It's best to attack
‪when the enemy least expects it,

156
00:10:56,447 --> 00:10:57,740
‪so right away.

157
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:02,203
‪Right now?

158
00:11:03,579 --> 00:11:04,747
‪This is Ok Gye-hui.

159
00:11:06,374 --> 00:11:08,167
‪Let's call an extraordinary
‪shareholders' meeting.

160
00:11:09,835 --> 00:11:10,795
‪The agenda is

161
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:14,882
‪the removal of Cheon Yeo-ri,
‪CEO of Reina Hotel.

162
00:11:24,266 --> 00:11:25,351
‪She isn't picking up.

163
00:11:25,434 --> 00:11:28,187
‪Ok Gye-hui knows no fear.

164
00:11:40,491 --> 00:11:41,742
‪I'm sorry.

165
00:11:41,826 --> 00:11:43,911
‪It ended up coming to this.

166
00:11:43,994 --> 00:11:45,371
‪No, I let my guard down too.

167
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:49,041
‪Who knew she'd strike
‪the day after your engagement ceremony?

168
00:11:49,917 --> 00:11:51,043
‪How are things looking?

169
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:54,004
‪Those loyal to the former chairman
‪have sided with Director Ok,

170
00:11:54,505 --> 00:11:56,132
‪putting us 3% behind in shares.

171
00:11:56,215 --> 00:12:00,594
‪In the end, it'll most likely come down
‪to a 51 to 49 split.

172
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:04,640
‪How about

173
00:12:05,391 --> 00:12:07,810
‪using the slush fund information
‪you obtained recently?

174
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:12,690
‪I've obtained information
‪that they amassed a slush fund

175
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:14,650
‪by purchasing artworks
‪to display in the hotel.

176
00:12:14,733 --> 00:12:17,027
‪Yeeon Museum of Art is involved,

177
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:19,697
‪and so is Ha-ri's uncle,
‪Chief Prosecutor Ok Gye-dong.

178
00:12:20,531 --> 00:12:22,992
‪That would work to our advantage.
‪Why not release it now?

179
00:12:23,075 --> 00:12:24,827
‪Everything is still circumstantial.

180
00:12:24,910 --> 00:12:27,788
‪We don't have anyone's confession
‪or proof to back the claim.

181
00:12:28,622 --> 00:12:31,750
‪If we release it rashly
‪at a critical time like this,

182
00:12:31,834 --> 00:12:33,669
‪we'll struggle to maintain
‪our stock price.

183
00:12:33,752 --> 00:12:37,131
‪And with Chief Prosecutor
‪Ok Gye-dong on their side,

184
00:12:37,214 --> 00:12:38,257
‪things could go badly

185
00:12:38,841 --> 00:12:41,427
‪and the hotel and I could become targets.

186
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:43,888
‪I do remember something similar happened

187
00:12:43,971 --> 00:12:45,681
‪during the former chairman's time.

188
00:12:46,390 --> 00:12:48,517
‪The truth will eventually come out,

189
00:12:49,143 --> 00:12:50,936
‪but it will take a long time.

190
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:54,440
‪In the meantime,
‪Reina and I'll be dragged through the mud.

191
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:57,234
‪Time isn't on our side.

192
00:13:00,070 --> 00:13:02,490
‪I'll request an investigation
‪when the time is right.

193
00:13:04,241 --> 00:13:06,160
‪Are there any shareholders
‪worth contacting?

194
00:13:06,243 --> 00:13:07,077
‪Here's the list.

195
00:13:12,875 --> 00:13:15,294
‪Let's contact as many as we can.

196
00:13:16,545 --> 00:13:18,130
‪You'll do it yourself, ma'am?

197
00:13:18,714 --> 00:13:20,466
‪I have to do whatever it takes.

198
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:27,097
‪Hello.

199
00:13:27,181 --> 00:13:28,724
‪This is Cheon Yeo-ri, CEO of Reina.

200
00:13:31,644 --> 00:13:32,811
‪How have you been?

201
00:13:33,521 --> 00:13:35,731
‪Hello, Chairman. It's Baek Gyeong-ja.

202
00:13:36,524 --> 00:13:37,858
‪Yes, I know.

203
00:13:38,526 --> 00:13:40,819
‪I should've kept them in line
‪while I could.

204
00:13:40,903 --> 00:13:43,072
‪I heard your child is clever and bright.

205
00:13:43,155 --> 00:13:46,700
‪I hope they learn a great deal
‪and join our company.

206
00:13:47,326 --> 00:13:48,786
‪Hi, Gang-uk.

207
00:13:48,869 --> 00:13:51,121
<i>‪Something came up at work.</i>

208
00:13:51,205 --> 00:13:53,290
‪Can I call you once things are settled?

209
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:56,001
‪Yes, of course.
‪Call me when you have time.

210
00:13:56,085 --> 00:13:57,044
‪Thanks.

211
00:13:58,879 --> 00:14:00,297
‪They're waiting for you inside.

212
00:14:02,591 --> 00:14:04,301
‪Hello. Sorry for the delay.

213
00:14:04,927 --> 00:14:05,886
‪Shall we sit down?

214
00:14:10,307 --> 00:14:11,392
<i>‪You've seen it once before,</i>

215
00:14:11,475 --> 00:14:14,144
‪how CEO Cheon's personal life
‪dragged down the stock price.

216
00:14:14,853 --> 00:14:15,938
‪Let's drink.

217
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:18,482
‪-Do give us your full support.
‪-Gosh.

218
00:14:19,441 --> 00:14:20,359
‪Don't worry, Chairwoman.

219
00:14:20,442 --> 00:14:22,278
‪-Everything will work out.
‪-Thank you.

220
00:14:22,361 --> 00:14:25,739
‪I'm sure you see
‪that she has her shortcomings,

221
00:14:25,823 --> 00:14:26,657
‪so I hope you'll…

222
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:28,993
‪No. Even so, sir--

223
00:14:42,172 --> 00:14:43,007
‪Come in.

224
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:51,891
‪Ma'am?

225
00:14:51,974 --> 00:14:53,767
‪Here's the information
‪you requested yesterday.

226
00:14:55,019 --> 00:14:56,437
‪-Mr. Bong.
‪-Yes?

227
00:14:57,855 --> 00:15:01,567
‪I'd like to contact her,
‪Han Se-in, in person.

228
00:15:01,650 --> 00:15:02,818
‪Yes, ma'am.

229
00:15:15,164 --> 00:15:16,040
‪Min-hwan.

230
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:18,292
‪You're here.

231
00:15:19,084 --> 00:15:22,171
‪What's the occasion,
‪asking me to keep you company?

232
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:25,174
‪You mind?

233
00:15:25,257 --> 00:15:26,884
‪Of course I don't.

234
00:15:27,384 --> 00:15:29,011
‪You're surrounded by people.

235
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:31,180
‪I'm surprised, that's all.

236
00:15:32,222 --> 00:15:34,391
‪You ignored so many of my calls until now.

237
00:15:35,684 --> 00:15:36,518
‪Sorry.

238
00:15:36,602 --> 00:15:38,562
‪I had a lot to sort out.

239
00:15:39,396 --> 00:15:41,690
‪So? Did you sort everything out?

240
00:15:42,983 --> 00:15:43,859
‪Almost.

241
00:15:44,818 --> 00:15:46,195
‪Does that include Yeo-ri?

242
00:15:49,531 --> 00:15:51,158
‪She must be having a tough time.

243
00:15:51,241 --> 00:15:53,202
‪She is in a tough situation,

244
00:15:53,285 --> 00:15:54,912
‪but I doubt things are bad for her.

245
00:15:55,496 --> 00:15:56,538
‪Look at her.

246
00:15:56,622 --> 00:15:58,874
‪Despite everything,
‪she quashed those rumors

247
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:00,292
‪and got engaged to that prosecutor.

248
00:16:01,085 --> 00:16:03,128
‪I do admire her resilience.

249
00:16:05,214 --> 00:16:06,131
‪How are you doing?

250
00:16:08,592 --> 00:16:09,468
‪Let's drink.

251
00:16:18,102 --> 00:16:20,604
‪You don't leave any openings, do you?

252
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:24,483
‪Neither do I.

253
00:16:27,194 --> 00:16:28,028
‪Min-hwan.

254
00:16:28,112 --> 00:16:30,072
‪If I were to replace Yeo-ri,

255
00:16:31,907 --> 00:16:32,783
‪would you date me?

256
00:16:34,868 --> 00:16:38,622
‪Yeo-ri will lose her position
‪after the shareholders' meeting.

257
00:16:39,206 --> 00:16:41,000
‪It won't be as easy as you think.

258
00:16:42,042 --> 00:16:43,002
‪She's Cheon Yeo-ri.

259
00:16:44,086 --> 00:16:45,462
‪Be honest with me.

260
00:16:46,296 --> 00:16:48,173
‪Is it that impossible to give up on her?

261
00:16:52,052 --> 00:16:53,095
‪When did it all begin?

262
00:16:56,432 --> 00:16:57,391
‪I'm not sure.

263
00:16:59,226 --> 00:17:00,686
‪Ever since I was young,

264
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:03,564
‪I've always worried
‪about other people's feelings.

265
00:17:04,732 --> 00:17:05,733
‪But with Yeo-ri…

266
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:11,739
‪I didn't have to do that,
‪and I could relax around her.

267
00:17:14,908 --> 00:17:16,702
‪That's why I grew to like her.

268
00:17:18,537 --> 00:17:20,748
‪I thought she'd always stay
‪right where she was.

269
00:17:21,415 --> 00:17:22,916
‪But when I came back…

270
00:17:27,337 --> 00:17:28,964
‪Before I give up for good…

271
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:34,011
‪It may seem reckless,
‪but I might try something different.

272
00:17:35,471 --> 00:17:38,015
‪It'll be my first and last attempt.

273
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:06,126
‪Ma'am, it's a call regarding Ms. Han.

274
00:18:09,046 --> 00:18:10,380
‪Hello, Cheon Yeo-ri speaking.

275
00:18:12,132 --> 00:18:13,509
‪She's out of the country?

276
00:18:14,301 --> 00:18:15,677
‪Then where is she?

277
00:18:19,431 --> 00:18:20,432
‪Yes.

278
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:24,144
‪Okay.

279
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:26,980
‪Is that so?

280
00:18:31,693 --> 00:18:33,487
‪You can reach her by phone though, right?

281
00:18:34,029 --> 00:18:36,115
‪Put me through
‪once you're able to reach her.

282
00:18:36,865 --> 00:18:37,783
‪Thanks.

283
00:18:45,415 --> 00:18:46,583
‪Gang-uk.

284
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:47,668
‪Yeo-ri.

285
00:18:55,259 --> 00:18:58,679
‪I tried to be patient and wait,

286
00:18:58,762 --> 00:19:01,348
‪but I couldn't reach you
‪when we'd just gotten engaged.

287
00:19:01,431 --> 00:19:02,599
‪And I missed you.

288
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:07,396
‪I was also worried
‪that something was wrong.

289
00:19:08,313 --> 00:19:09,314
‪Yeo-ri.

290
00:19:09,857 --> 00:19:12,276
‪Did I do something wrong?

291
00:19:14,862 --> 00:19:16,822
‪Is that what you were worried about?

292
00:19:18,365 --> 00:19:20,951
‪I'm sorry. I should've called you.

293
00:19:22,744 --> 00:19:23,871
‪What's going on?

294
00:19:25,873 --> 00:19:28,208
‪It's not in the news yet,

295
00:19:28,292 --> 00:19:32,045
‪but an extraordinary shareholders' meeting
‪will be held at Reina soon.

296
00:19:32,129 --> 00:19:34,715
‪The main agenda will be my removal.

297
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:37,885
‪That's why things were a bit crazy.

298
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:40,971
‪Oh, I see. I'm sorry.

299
00:19:41,054 --> 00:19:44,266
‪I thought our engagement
‪helped secure your position.

300
00:19:45,726 --> 00:19:47,019
‪Is it a serious situation?

301
00:19:47,102 --> 00:19:50,480
‪I'm trying my best
‪to persuade the shareholders,

302
00:19:51,064 --> 00:19:52,357
‪but things don't look great.

303
00:19:53,066 --> 00:19:55,652
‪It looks like I might have to
‪stay here all night.

304
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:57,946
‪I'll stay with you.

305
00:20:00,949 --> 00:20:02,784
‪No. You can't do that.

306
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:05,621
‪Why not? I belong right by your side.

307
00:20:05,704 --> 00:20:08,040
‪If there's not much I can do,
‪I'll run coffee errands.

308
00:20:08,123 --> 00:20:09,291
‪I make pretty good coffee.

309
00:20:17,716 --> 00:20:18,884
‪CEO CHEON YEO-RI

310
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:22,721
‪FRIENDLY, HOSTILE, NEUTRAL

311
00:20:26,516 --> 00:20:29,019
‪Yeo-ri. You can take your gloves off
‪when you're with me.

312
00:20:29,102 --> 00:20:30,062
‪I'll be careful.

313
00:20:33,941 --> 00:20:34,775
‪Okay.

314
00:20:39,905 --> 00:20:42,491
‪Who is this person that you're so…

315
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:45,327
‪REINA HOLDINGS
‪MAJOR SHAREHOLDERS CHECKLIST

316
00:20:45,410 --> 00:20:49,248
‪CKO Construction is one of
‪Reina Holdings' major shareholders.

317
00:20:49,831 --> 00:20:52,376
‪One of the chairman's sons got divorced

318
00:20:52,918 --> 00:20:55,128
‪and the former daughter-in-law
‪received some shares.

319
00:20:56,797 --> 00:20:58,632
‪-That's Han Se-in?
‪-Yeah.

320
00:20:59,383 --> 00:21:02,803
‪So I'm gathering information
‪to find a way to win her over.

321
00:21:02,886 --> 00:21:05,055
‪Her father is Han Jeong-eup.

322
00:21:06,348 --> 00:21:08,016
‪I heard that name somewhere.

323
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:09,685
‪Do you know Chaeum Artrion?

324
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:10,936
‪He built that.

325
00:21:11,019 --> 00:21:14,439
‪I know. My mom took me there
‪to see shows when I was young.

326
00:21:15,148 --> 00:21:16,775
‪As an adult,
‪I went a few times with my grandma.

327
00:21:17,859 --> 00:21:20,737
‪She must have
‪a lot of memories there with you.

328
00:21:20,821 --> 00:21:22,864
‪Of course. She loved going there.

329
00:21:25,492 --> 00:21:28,453
‪Since CKO Construction is owned
‪by her former in-laws,

330
00:21:28,537 --> 00:21:31,915
‪I'm hoping Ms. Han
‪will make a different vote.

331
00:21:32,582 --> 00:21:34,126
‪So I'm waiting to hear from her.

332
00:22:31,850 --> 00:22:33,185
‪Ma'am!

333
00:22:33,268 --> 00:22:34,394
‪Ma'am.

334
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:40,525
‪I didn't see anything.

335
00:22:41,109 --> 00:22:42,277
‪But that's not what's important.

336
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:45,072
‪Ms. Han is currently residing
‪in Singapore.

337
00:22:45,906 --> 00:22:46,740
‪What?

338
00:22:46,823 --> 00:22:49,576
‪She runs her own business there

339
00:22:49,659 --> 00:22:51,578
‪and actively holds exhibitions too.

340
00:22:52,412 --> 00:22:54,122
‪What kind of exhibitions do you mean?

341
00:22:54,206 --> 00:22:55,749
‪Well, I heard…

342
00:22:55,832 --> 00:22:58,043
‪She's an art director
‪or something of the kind.

343
00:22:58,126 --> 00:22:58,960
‪It's all here.

344
00:23:01,755 --> 00:23:04,174
‪Her name is also on the list of attendees

345
00:23:04,257 --> 00:23:07,344
‪of the hotel investment conference
‪that you held off on attending.

346
00:23:08,887 --> 00:23:09,721
‪Is that so?

347
00:23:11,014 --> 00:23:13,100
‪Put me through to her
‪as soon as you reach her.

348
00:23:13,683 --> 00:23:14,810
‪Yes, will do.

349
00:23:14,893 --> 00:23:15,977
‪I'll see myself out then.

350
00:23:22,234 --> 00:23:25,695
‪She seems to be closely aligned
‪with our interests.

351
00:23:28,990 --> 00:23:30,158
‪I think we've got a good shot.

352
00:23:56,768 --> 00:23:57,853
‪Ma'am, I'm coming in!

353
00:24:00,355 --> 00:24:01,773
‪I'm sorry, ma'am.

354
00:24:02,607 --> 00:24:05,527
‪We got a call from Ms. Han.

355
00:24:10,782 --> 00:24:11,741
‪Hello.

356
00:24:11,825 --> 00:24:13,118
‪This is Cheon Yeo-ri of Reina.

357
00:24:15,495 --> 00:24:17,205
‪I'm going abroad on a business trip.

358
00:24:18,248 --> 00:24:21,835
‪I understand that it's a conference
‪to attract investors,

359
00:24:21,918 --> 00:24:24,671
‪but why go now
‪if it won't bring immediate results?

360
00:24:25,505 --> 00:24:26,506
‪Are you confident you can manage?

361
00:24:27,632 --> 00:24:28,466
‪Yes.

362
00:24:29,384 --> 00:24:30,844
‪Please keep up the work on your end.

363
00:24:30,927 --> 00:24:33,305
‪I'll stay in touch
‪with any shareholders I can reach,

364
00:24:33,388 --> 00:24:34,764
‪even while I'm abroad.

365
00:24:34,848 --> 00:24:37,058
‪Will you be able to return on time?

366
00:24:39,644 --> 00:24:40,478
‪Of course.

367
00:24:43,565 --> 00:24:45,734
<i>‪Yeo-ri's going abroad for business</i>
<i>‪at a time like this?</i>

368
00:24:45,817 --> 00:24:48,445
‪I got an invitation to it too.

369
00:24:49,154 --> 00:24:53,366
‪It is a pretty large-scale conference
‪as far as attracting investment goes.

370
00:24:53,450 --> 00:24:55,243
‪I get why she wants to go,

371
00:24:56,036 --> 00:24:58,371
‪but why go now at a time like this?

372
00:24:58,455 --> 00:25:01,791
‪Yeo-ri must feel cornered
‪to resort to something this ridiculous.

373
00:25:01,875 --> 00:25:05,170
‪She'd likely lose her position
‪if the vote were tomorrow.

374
00:25:05,253 --> 00:25:07,923
‪Even if she makes a deal there,
‪she'd only have time to sign an MOU.

375
00:25:09,132 --> 00:25:10,383
‪It's quite an odd move.

376
00:25:12,427 --> 00:25:13,470
‪Have our people look into it.

377
00:25:14,804 --> 00:25:17,015
‪This is the list of attendees
‪for the Singapore conference.

378
00:25:18,767 --> 00:25:21,686
‪The sole agenda of the upcoming
‪general meeting is her removal,

379
00:25:22,312 --> 00:25:24,272
‪yet she's traveling abroad for business?

380
00:25:25,565 --> 00:25:28,568
‪Compile a list of shareholders
‪who recently transferred their shares.

381
00:25:28,652 --> 00:25:29,736
‪Yes, sir.

382
00:25:37,285 --> 00:25:40,789
‪I'm too worried about you
‪going abroad on your own.

383
00:25:41,998 --> 00:25:44,626
‪There's nothing to worry about.
‪I'll be just fine.

384
00:25:44,709 --> 00:25:47,254
‪No, not about you.
‪I'm worried about myself.

385
00:25:48,713 --> 00:25:52,259
‪I'm already dreading the thought
‪of not seeing you for days.

386
00:25:52,801 --> 00:25:54,177
<i>‪Then come with me.</i>

387
00:25:54,261 --> 00:25:56,554
‪Don't prosecutors go abroad
‪on business trips?

388
00:25:56,638 --> 00:26:00,600
‪There are global seminars and conferences.
‪Should I actually look into it?

389
00:26:01,559 --> 00:26:03,979
‪Leave it. I won't be away for long.

390
00:26:04,729 --> 00:26:05,814
‪Okay.

391
00:26:05,897 --> 00:26:07,440
‪Yeo-ri.

392
00:26:07,524 --> 00:26:10,235
‪I'll come to the airport to see you off.

393
00:26:17,367 --> 00:26:19,369
‪Man, I barely finished it in time.

394
00:26:20,787 --> 00:26:21,621
‪Hold on.

395
00:26:23,248 --> 00:26:24,165
‪There's more?

396
00:26:24,833 --> 00:26:25,667
‪Silly me.

397
00:26:25,750 --> 00:26:28,336
‪-You should've handed it over earlier.
‪-Mr. Ma.

398
00:26:29,337 --> 00:26:30,297
‪What's all that?

399
00:26:30,380 --> 00:26:32,882
‪The Case Division assigned us some cases.

400
00:26:32,966 --> 00:26:34,718
‪Why today, of all days…

401
00:26:36,094 --> 00:26:36,970
‪Oh, man.

402
00:26:37,554 --> 00:26:38,596
‪Come on!

403
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:40,682
‪Why are there so many?

404
00:26:40,765 --> 00:26:43,601
‪Ms. Eom is already there
‪and arranging meetings on her end.

405
00:26:43,685 --> 00:26:44,853
‪I'll keep you updated

406
00:26:44,936 --> 00:26:47,814
‪if anything needs to be arranged
‪on this end.

407
00:26:48,398 --> 00:26:51,359
‪Take good care of my grandmother
‪until I come back.

408
00:26:51,443 --> 00:26:53,695
‪Please don't worry.
‪Remember, I'm Bong Ji-uk.

409
00:26:54,988 --> 00:26:56,156
‪Ma'am.

410
00:26:57,532 --> 00:26:58,950
‪Good luck.

411
00:27:00,285 --> 00:27:01,119
‪Thank you.

412
00:27:01,703 --> 00:27:02,537
‪Of course.

413
00:27:02,620 --> 00:27:03,663
‪-Yeo-ri.
‪-Oh.

414
00:27:04,414 --> 00:27:05,582
‪-Gang-uk.
‪-Hello.

415
00:27:05,665 --> 00:27:07,000
‪Hello.

416
00:27:08,793 --> 00:27:10,420
‪-Mr. Bong, wait.
‪-Yes?

417
00:27:12,047 --> 00:27:13,465
‪Oh, dear. Sorry.

418
00:27:17,719 --> 00:27:19,179
‪Weren't you busy with work?

419
00:27:19,262 --> 00:27:22,932
‪Don't worry about my work.
‪I'd take you to Singapore if I could.

420
00:27:27,771 --> 00:27:28,605
‪Huh?

421
00:27:29,230 --> 00:27:30,065
‪What's going on?

422
00:27:30,148 --> 00:27:31,900
‪Why? What is it?

423
00:27:37,072 --> 00:27:38,073
‪Is Kang Min-hwan going too?

424
00:27:42,118 --> 00:27:43,745
‪I didn't know he was going.

425
00:27:46,956 --> 00:27:48,041
‪Should I go too?

426
00:27:49,459 --> 00:27:51,669
‪I think I should come with you.

427
00:27:53,463 --> 00:27:54,547
‪Don't be silly.

428
00:27:55,256 --> 00:27:56,633
‪I'll be fine.

429
00:27:57,217 --> 00:27:58,802
‪Call me if something happens, okay?

430
00:27:58,885 --> 00:28:00,637
‪I'll fly right over to see you.

431
00:28:01,137 --> 00:28:02,180
‪Promise me, okay?

432
00:28:02,722 --> 00:28:03,556
‪Sure.

433
00:28:04,641 --> 00:28:07,394
‪-Hyeong-min, that thing from last time.
‪-What?

434
00:28:07,477 --> 00:28:10,230
‪Is this year's International Association
‪of Prosecutors event in Singapore?

435
00:28:10,313 --> 00:28:12,649
‪It has to be, okay? Pull up the notice.

436
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:15,860
‪-Yeah, that one.
‪-It is happening in Singapore.

437
00:28:15,944 --> 00:28:18,071
‪"Prosecution organizations
‪and personnel from around the world

438
00:28:18,154 --> 00:28:20,615
‪gather to discuss
‪ideal criminal legislation."

439
00:28:20,698 --> 00:28:22,951
‪It's open to well-rounded prosecutors.

440
00:28:23,034 --> 00:28:24,452
‪That's me. This is perfect.

441
00:28:24,536 --> 00:28:26,204
‪Sign me up immediately.

442
00:28:26,287 --> 00:28:28,665
‪Forget it.
‪Don't even dream of going abroad.

443
00:28:28,748 --> 00:28:32,335
‪You refused to go because
‪you didn't want to write an extra report.

444
00:28:32,419 --> 00:28:33,420
‪No, not anymore.

445
00:28:33,503 --> 00:28:36,047
‪I'll write up a killer report.
‪Hyeong-min, sign me up right now.

446
00:28:36,131 --> 00:28:37,465
‪-I can't.
‪-What?

447
00:28:37,549 --> 00:28:39,175
‪Applications were due yesterday.

448
00:28:43,263 --> 00:28:45,932
‪There's a conference in Thailand
‪to review international law.

449
00:28:46,015 --> 00:28:47,308
‪Yes, there is.

450
00:28:47,392 --> 00:28:49,352
‪Call up the organization hosting that

451
00:28:49,436 --> 00:28:51,396
‪and have them host it
‪in Singapore instead, okay?

452
00:28:51,938 --> 00:28:52,772
‪What?

453
00:28:52,856 --> 00:28:55,608
‪Let's say they move it to Singapore
‪and all you have to do is go.

454
00:28:55,692 --> 00:28:56,985
‪But today is your turn

455
00:28:57,777 --> 00:28:58,778
‪to handle the night shift.

456
00:28:59,654 --> 00:29:00,488
‪You forgot?

457
00:29:01,698 --> 00:29:02,741
‪Oh, jeez.

458
00:29:03,575 --> 00:29:04,409
‪You forgot.

459
00:29:04,909 --> 00:29:06,077
‪Oh, jeez.

460
00:30:00,673 --> 00:30:01,591
‪Let's go, sir.

461
00:30:08,473 --> 00:30:10,225
‪Will you attend the reception later?

462
00:30:10,683 --> 00:30:12,143
‪Most of the investors will be there.

463
00:30:13,645 --> 00:30:15,063
‪Of course. I'll be there.

464
00:30:33,081 --> 00:30:33,915
‪Hello?

465
00:30:33,998 --> 00:30:36,376
‪Ma'am, I just heard from Ms. Han.

466
00:30:36,459 --> 00:30:37,752
‪She wants to meet you an hour later.

467
00:30:38,753 --> 00:30:39,963
‪Did she say why?

468
00:30:40,046 --> 00:30:42,507
‪I asked, but she only said
‪it was personal.

469
00:30:43,299 --> 00:30:45,593
<i>‪I didn't want to upset her</i>
<i>‪before negotiations,</i>

470
00:30:45,677 --> 00:30:47,512
‪so I said you'd agree to the delay.

471
00:30:47,595 --> 00:30:48,471
‪I apologize.

472
00:30:48,555 --> 00:30:50,348
‪I understand. Bye.

473
00:31:20,378 --> 00:31:21,379
‪Are you Ms. Cheon?

474
00:31:23,006 --> 00:31:24,757
‪Hello, Ms. Han.

475
00:31:29,137 --> 00:31:32,098
‪I was surprised to get your call.

476
00:31:32,682 --> 00:31:35,602
‪You came all the way here
‪to meet me over my 3% stake?

477
00:31:37,186 --> 00:31:39,147
‪I wanted to meet you in person.

478
00:31:44,569 --> 00:31:46,487
‪I did some research myself.

479
00:31:47,530 --> 00:31:48,907
‪Some want you removed

480
00:31:48,990 --> 00:31:52,410
‪because of your scandals
‪and poor management skills.

481
00:31:56,122 --> 00:32:00,460
‪I can't say I've been perfect
‪at every turn,

482
00:32:00,543 --> 00:32:02,879
‪but I can't accept the claim

483
00:32:02,962 --> 00:32:06,758
‪that I mismanaged the company
‪enough to warrant a removal motion.

484
00:32:07,759 --> 00:32:10,178
‪I can prove it with objective numbers.

485
00:32:11,554 --> 00:32:12,889
‪Would you take a look?

486
00:32:21,189 --> 00:32:22,357
‪I'll be honest with you.

487
00:32:23,191 --> 00:32:24,108
‪The truth is,

488
00:32:24,901 --> 00:32:30,031
‪someone made me a bold offer
‪just an hour ago.

489
00:32:31,324 --> 00:32:33,701
‪They offered double
‪the current market price for my shares.

490
00:32:36,329 --> 00:32:38,998
‪-They offered double?
‪-So I agreed to transfer them.

491
00:32:39,791 --> 00:32:40,708
‪What?

492
00:32:43,294 --> 00:32:45,088
‪Was it one of Director Ok's people?

493
00:32:45,171 --> 00:32:46,214
‪No.

494
00:32:47,423 --> 00:32:51,302
‪I have to keep their identity undisclosed
‪until the deal is signed.

495
00:32:52,804 --> 00:32:54,806
‪From my perspective,

496
00:32:54,889 --> 00:32:56,557
‪I have no reason to turn down the offer.

497
00:32:57,392 --> 00:32:58,267
‪Ms. Han.

498
00:32:58,351 --> 00:32:59,477
‪From what I see,

499
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:02,814
‪it's just a mudslinging fight
‪between family members.

500
00:33:02,897 --> 00:33:05,817
‪Doesn't it all end up the same,
‪whoever becomes CEO?

501
00:33:06,401 --> 00:33:09,445
‪You must know how things are, Ms. Han.

502
00:33:10,279 --> 00:33:11,406
‪Fights like these.

503
00:33:12,115 --> 00:33:14,701
‪You went through a legal dispute
‪with your younger brother.

504
00:33:15,952 --> 00:33:19,497
‪Let's leave my family out of this
‪when it's about yours.

505
00:33:21,165 --> 00:33:23,334
‪To be truthful, I have no interest

506
00:33:24,002 --> 00:33:25,837
‪in your fight to defend your position.

507
00:33:25,920 --> 00:33:28,965
‪I'm busy enough
‪running my own business here.

508
00:33:29,048 --> 00:33:31,759
‪I'm here for your business
‪interests as well.

509
00:33:32,969 --> 00:33:34,095
‪I don't see you

510
00:33:35,013 --> 00:33:38,975
‪as a mere shareholder
‪or someone whose shares I need to acquire.

511
00:33:39,600 --> 00:33:41,436
‪I want us to build our careers together

512
00:33:42,103 --> 00:33:44,397
‪through our shared passion for art.

513
00:33:45,106 --> 00:33:47,275
‪If you side with me this time,

514
00:33:47,358 --> 00:33:50,987
‪I'll give you the right to curate
‪and host exhibitions anywhere you want.

515
00:33:51,070 --> 00:33:52,780
‪That includes both

516
00:33:53,531 --> 00:33:55,908
‪Reina's domestic and overseas affiliates.

517
00:33:57,326 --> 00:33:58,703
‪With such authority,

518
00:33:58,786 --> 00:34:01,914
‪you may not be able to
‪double your investment right away,

519
00:34:01,998 --> 00:34:05,626
‪but the profit you stand to gain
‪in a few years will be much greater.

520
00:34:12,592 --> 00:34:15,094
‪That is a very alluring offer.

521
00:34:15,803 --> 00:34:17,472
‪It could boost my career too.

522
00:34:18,514 --> 00:34:22,018
‪But I care more about my immediate reality

523
00:34:22,101 --> 00:34:23,603
‪than the distant future.

524
00:34:24,979 --> 00:34:27,690
‪Thank you for the offer,
‪but I'll have to decline.

525
00:34:28,483 --> 00:34:30,276
‪-Ms. Han.
‪-I'm sorry.

526
00:34:31,652 --> 00:34:33,196
‪Just a moment.

527
00:34:34,822 --> 00:34:36,699
‪Can you hear me out a little more

528
00:34:37,617 --> 00:34:39,660
‪before you make up your mind?

529
00:34:40,244 --> 00:34:42,872
‪Well, I've already made up my mind.

530
00:34:44,040 --> 00:34:47,376
‪I don't think talking any further
‪will change anything.

531
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:49,378
‪But still…

532
00:35:03,976 --> 00:35:05,311
‪Are you all right, ma'am?

533
00:35:08,439 --> 00:35:12,735
‪Find out if Ms. Han will
‪attend the reception tonight.

534
00:35:13,402 --> 00:35:16,280
‪I already checked.
‪Her name is on the list.

535
00:36:44,702 --> 00:36:45,578
‪Are you all right?

536
00:36:46,704 --> 00:36:47,997
‪I heard your company's struggling.

537
00:36:50,499 --> 00:36:53,502
‪The company is fine.
‪I'm the one struggling.

538
00:36:54,086 --> 00:36:55,504
‪That's why I came all this way.

539
00:36:56,923 --> 00:36:59,050
‪I'm sure you'll manage.
‪You're Cheon Yeo-ri.

540
00:37:10,853 --> 00:37:13,231
<i>‪Apparently, it's some kind of</i>
<i>‪mystical object.</i>

541
00:37:14,232 --> 00:37:15,066
<i>‪Ji-hwan!</i>

542
00:37:18,236 --> 00:37:19,278
<i>‪You have to live.</i>

543
00:37:19,779 --> 00:37:21,030
<i>‪I'll die instead.</i>

544
00:37:26,494 --> 00:37:29,747
‪12 YEARS AGO

545
00:37:29,830 --> 00:37:30,873
‪Hold this for me.

546
00:37:34,001 --> 00:37:35,753
‪Oh, come on. In this day and age,

547
00:37:35,836 --> 00:37:38,881
‪you really think wearing that
‪will keep ghosts away?

548
00:37:40,591 --> 00:37:44,220
‪Look. My grandma said something
‪about this pendant.

549
00:37:44,303 --> 00:37:47,098
‪Apparently, it's some kind of
‪mystical object.

550
00:37:48,641 --> 00:37:50,685
‪Hey, I'm being serious.

551
00:37:50,768 --> 00:37:53,354
‪My grandma acts like
‪it's the end of the world

552
00:37:53,437 --> 00:37:54,689
‪if I so much as take it off.

553
00:37:55,273 --> 00:37:58,401
‪Well, it's not like
‪there's no way to confirm it.

554
00:37:58,985 --> 00:38:00,027
‪I believe you.

555
00:38:00,736 --> 00:38:02,905
‪Why don't you try wearing it?

556
00:38:03,948 --> 00:38:06,075
‪-Me?
‪-I have a feeling

557
00:38:06,158 --> 00:38:08,160
‪it'll suit you way better than me.

558
00:38:10,788 --> 00:38:12,290
‪You know, necklaces like this

559
00:38:12,873 --> 00:38:15,209
‪look better when worn by someone pretty.

560
00:38:16,585 --> 00:38:17,795
‪It looks great on you.

561
00:38:18,379 --> 00:38:19,213
‪You can keep it.

562
00:38:19,797 --> 00:38:20,631
‪Really?

563
00:38:21,424 --> 00:38:24,302
‪But what if something happens to you?

564
00:38:26,470 --> 00:38:27,763
‪That's just my luck then.

565
00:38:27,847 --> 00:38:29,890
‪I don't mind it
‪if it means I can save you.

566
00:38:31,309 --> 00:38:33,602
‪-What?
‪-If something does happen,

567
00:38:35,730 --> 00:38:37,815
‪you have to live. I'll die instead.

568
00:38:40,234 --> 00:38:41,861
‪Why would you say something like that?

569
00:38:46,324 --> 00:38:48,617
‪Are you okay? Oh, jeez.

570
00:38:49,118 --> 00:38:51,412
‪Wait here.
‪I'll get something to wipe you dry.

571
00:38:51,495 --> 00:38:52,371
‪Okay.

572
00:38:54,165 --> 00:38:55,249
‪Is something wrong?

573
00:38:55,333 --> 00:38:56,584
‪Let me see…

574
00:38:56,667 --> 00:38:58,502
‪-Do we have any tissues?
‪-Tissues?

575
00:38:58,586 --> 00:38:59,837
‪I don't know. I don't see any.

576
00:38:59,920 --> 00:39:00,963
‪There aren't any here.

577
00:39:23,903 --> 00:39:24,904
‪Ji-hwan!

578
00:39:31,077 --> 00:39:31,994
<i>‪Yeo-ri!</i>

579
00:39:32,078 --> 00:39:33,913
<i>‪What if something happens to you?</i>

580
00:39:34,413 --> 00:39:36,040
<i>‪I don't mind it</i>
<i>‪if it means I can save you.</i>

581
00:39:36,123 --> 00:39:37,833
<i>‪If something does happen,</i>

582
00:39:38,959 --> 00:39:41,504
<i>‪you have to live. I'll die instead.</i>

583
00:39:48,469 --> 00:39:49,553
<i>‪The pendant.</i>

584
00:39:51,722 --> 00:39:52,723
‪Are you okay?

585
00:39:54,392 --> 00:39:55,643
‪Yeah.

586
00:39:59,647 --> 00:40:00,856
‪I'd forgotten…

587
00:40:02,191 --> 00:40:05,361
‪a lot of the memories from back then.

588
00:40:07,113 --> 00:40:08,531
‪Do you remember Ji-hwan's pendant

589
00:40:09,323 --> 00:40:10,908
‪from the accident 12 years ago?

590
00:40:14,870 --> 00:40:16,288
‪What pendant?

591
00:40:16,914 --> 00:40:20,209
‪The necklace.
‪Ji-hwan put it on me that day.

592
00:40:21,252 --> 00:40:22,503
‪I was wearing it.

593
00:40:25,172 --> 00:40:28,300
‪Do you know if it was
‪among his belongings?

594
00:40:30,302 --> 00:40:31,220
‪I'm not sure.

595
00:40:32,596 --> 00:40:34,140
‪If you were wearing it,

596
00:40:34,223 --> 00:40:36,058
‪maybe you lost it
‪when you fell into the sea?

597
00:40:39,478 --> 00:40:40,438
‪Did I?

598
00:40:45,401 --> 00:40:46,318
‪Ma'am.

599
00:40:49,196 --> 00:40:50,072
‪Excuse me.

600
00:40:53,742 --> 00:40:54,910
‪It's about Ms. Han.

601
00:40:54,994 --> 00:40:57,246
‪She checked out of the hotel
‪30 minutes before this reception.

602
00:40:58,247 --> 00:40:59,123
‪What?

603
00:41:08,966 --> 00:41:09,800
‪Let's go.

604
00:41:16,515 --> 00:41:20,895
‪Ms. Cheon was in continued contact
‪with a woman named Han Se-in in Singapore.

605
00:41:22,938 --> 00:41:23,814
‪CKO CONSTRUCTION, HAN SE-IN, NEUTRAL

606
00:41:23,898 --> 00:41:24,982
‪She owns exactly 3%.

607
00:41:26,734 --> 00:41:30,696
‪I'm quite surprised and also flustered.

608
00:41:31,822 --> 00:41:34,533
‪You're offering double the market price?

609
00:41:34,617 --> 00:41:36,243
‪A card has the greatest impact

610
00:41:36,327 --> 00:41:39,163
‪when it's played
‪at the most unexpected moment.

611
00:41:39,747 --> 00:41:40,748
‪That is true.

612
00:41:41,415 --> 00:41:42,708
‪So is this the reason

613
00:41:43,542 --> 00:41:46,879
‪you asked me to delay my meeting
‪with Ms. Cheon by an hour?

614
00:41:46,962 --> 00:41:48,506
‪A deal is best when offered first.

615
00:41:49,924 --> 00:41:51,217
‪I have just one condition.

616
00:41:51,300 --> 00:41:53,135
‪Until the deal is finalized,

617
00:41:53,636 --> 00:41:55,888
‪you are to keep
‪the buyer's identity undisclosed.

618
00:41:56,805 --> 00:41:58,182
<i>‪That's all I ask.</i>

619
00:42:00,976 --> 00:42:02,102
‪Have you called her?

620
00:42:02,186 --> 00:42:04,855
‪She's not answering.
‪I think she's avoiding the calls.

621
00:42:05,814 --> 00:42:07,525
‪First, call Mr. Bong.

622
00:42:08,150 --> 00:42:11,946
‪Tell him to put a team together
‪and find out what Ms. Han is up to.

623
00:42:12,029 --> 00:42:13,197
‪Yes, ma'am.

624
00:42:13,280 --> 00:42:14,365
‪Wait a minute.

625
00:42:16,075 --> 00:42:20,371
‪Ms. Han has nothing to do
‪with hotel investment.

626
00:42:22,414 --> 00:42:24,041
‪Yet she was invited to this event.

627
00:42:24,124 --> 00:42:27,211
‪I'll look into who invited her here.

628
00:42:47,982 --> 00:42:49,024
‪I love this.

629
00:42:54,613 --> 00:42:55,489
‪Is this much okay?

630
00:43:04,081 --> 00:43:06,083
‪Man, it's not here. Where is it?

631
00:43:10,212 --> 00:43:11,130
‪What's this?

632
00:43:12,756 --> 00:43:14,091
‪He never said a word to me.

633
00:43:30,107 --> 00:43:30,983
‪Give me that.

634
00:43:33,360 --> 00:43:34,945
‪Why do you have this?

635
00:43:35,529 --> 00:43:37,114
‪-Do you…
‪-It's not like that.

636
00:43:38,240 --> 00:43:39,450
‪What do you mean?

637
00:43:40,534 --> 00:43:41,535
‪Min-hwan.

638
00:43:43,120 --> 00:43:44,580
‪Have you lied to me all along?

639
00:43:47,541 --> 00:43:48,792
‪What did I lie about?

640
00:43:51,003 --> 00:43:52,630
‪You asked me if I'd asked Yeo-ri out.

641
00:43:54,256 --> 00:43:55,633
‪You said the matching rings were too much.

642
00:43:56,675 --> 00:43:59,136
‪You lied whenever I asked
‪because you had an ulterior motive.

643
00:43:59,720 --> 00:44:01,013
‪I didn't lie about anything.

644
00:44:02,431 --> 00:44:04,850
‪And I don't have to explain
‪my feelings to you.

645
00:44:08,562 --> 00:44:10,481
‪I don't want to argue with you about this.

646
00:44:11,607 --> 00:44:13,275
‪That's your problem.

647
00:44:14,068 --> 00:44:15,861
‪If there's something wrong, talk about it.

648
00:44:15,944 --> 00:44:17,279
‪Why do you always avoid the situation?

649
00:44:24,870 --> 00:44:26,163
‪Min-hwan.

650
00:44:26,246 --> 00:44:27,164
‪Min-hwan!

651
00:44:29,541 --> 00:44:30,459
‪Min-hwan!

652
00:44:31,627 --> 00:44:32,628
‪Kang Min-hwan.

653
00:44:33,253 --> 00:44:35,673
‪Want me to tell you
‪why I avoid the situation?

654
00:44:37,049 --> 00:44:38,676
‪I can argue with you about anything,

655
00:44:39,343 --> 00:44:40,803
‪but nothing will change.

656
00:44:41,387 --> 00:44:42,304
‪What won't change?

657
00:44:42,388 --> 00:44:44,098
‪If I so much as raise my voice at you,

658
00:44:45,265 --> 00:44:47,017
‪do you know how our family looks at me?

659
00:44:48,769 --> 00:44:49,895
‪What do you mean?

660
00:44:53,399 --> 00:44:55,192
‪Tell me. How do they look at you?

661
00:45:00,406 --> 00:45:02,616
‪Forget it. I've had enough.

662
00:45:03,534 --> 00:45:05,202
‪Do you have some kind of victim mentality?

663
00:45:08,122 --> 00:45:08,997
‪What?

664
00:45:10,624 --> 00:45:12,167
‪What's wrong?

665
00:45:32,479 --> 00:45:34,565
‪It's still a zero-sum game.

666
00:45:34,648 --> 00:45:37,526
‪If we take shares from them,
‪they take shares from us.

667
00:45:37,609 --> 00:45:39,945
‪We still don't know
‪what Ms. Han is up to, do we?

668
00:45:43,115 --> 00:45:44,158
‪Yes.

669
00:45:44,241 --> 00:45:45,451
‪Keep looking into it.

670
00:45:46,201 --> 00:45:47,035
‪Bye.

671
00:46:25,491 --> 00:46:26,450
‪INCOMING CALL

672
00:46:26,533 --> 00:46:27,701
‪Hello? Yeo-ri?

673
00:46:29,036 --> 00:46:30,871
‪You're still awake.

674
00:46:30,954 --> 00:46:33,332
‪I was worried you'd be asleep.

675
00:46:33,415 --> 00:46:34,750
<i>‪I wouldn't be asleep.</i>

676
00:46:34,833 --> 00:46:36,543
‪How are things going on your end?

677
00:46:37,669 --> 00:46:40,005
‪Not too well, to be honest.

678
00:46:40,589 --> 00:46:42,841
<i>‪She turned me down at our first meeting,</i>

679
00:46:42,925 --> 00:46:45,135
‪and she's been ignoring us since then.

680
00:46:45,761 --> 00:46:47,846
‪She left without a trace.

681
00:46:47,930 --> 00:46:51,225
‪Man, that's not good.
‪You must've been flustered.

682
00:46:53,352 --> 00:46:55,187
‪Which is why, Gang-uk,

683
00:46:55,270 --> 00:46:56,897
‪I need to ask for a favor.

684
00:46:58,023 --> 00:47:00,567
‪I gave it a lot of thought
‪before calling you.

685
00:47:00,651 --> 00:47:03,987
‪Of course, tell me what you need.
‪I'll help with anything.

686
00:47:06,532 --> 00:47:10,661
‪First, there's something
‪I'd like you to pass to my secretary.

687
00:47:10,744 --> 00:47:13,622
‪-Okay.
<i>‪-And the other favor is…</i>

688
00:47:14,331 --> 00:47:18,919
‪Could you help us locate Han Se-in?

689
00:47:19,503 --> 00:47:22,005
<i>‪I do have a team looking for her,</i>

690
00:47:22,089 --> 00:47:24,174
‪but we're short on time.

691
00:47:24,258 --> 00:47:25,384
‪I can totally do that.

692
00:47:25,467 --> 00:47:27,219
‪I know a guy
‪whose specialty is finding people.

693
00:47:27,302 --> 00:47:28,887
‪I'll call him right away.

694
00:47:29,680 --> 00:47:30,514
‪Thank--

695
00:47:40,524 --> 00:47:42,442
‪What's this about?

696
00:47:42,526 --> 00:47:44,778
‪Hyeong-min,
‪I'm all sorts of urgent right now.

697
00:47:44,861 --> 00:47:47,864
‪I racked my brain
‪and you're the only one I could think of.

698
00:47:47,948 --> 00:47:49,157
‪What do you want me to do?

699
00:47:49,241 --> 00:47:51,451
‪-No way. I won't do it.
‪-Come on.

700
00:47:51,535 --> 00:47:55,038
‪From the sushi restaurant nearby
‪that you love so much,

701
00:47:55,122 --> 00:47:57,666
‪I brought an assortment
‪of the freshest-looking sushi.

702
00:47:58,375 --> 00:47:59,376
‪Look.

703
00:47:59,459 --> 00:48:01,920
‪-Mr. Ma, what do you take me for?
‪-Yeah?

704
00:48:02,004 --> 00:48:04,214
‪Do you think
‪a few pieces of sushi would…

705
00:48:04,798 --> 00:48:07,342
‪-Shall I have a taste?
‪-Yeah. Sit down.

706
00:48:07,426 --> 00:48:08,802
‪-Is this it?
‪-Yeah, that's it.

707
00:48:12,472 --> 00:48:13,640
‪BREATHING NEW LIFE INTO OLD PAINTINGS

708
00:48:16,393 --> 00:48:17,269
‪Here, open wide.

709
00:48:18,520 --> 00:48:19,730
‪Okay.

710
00:48:19,813 --> 00:48:21,148
‪Want the eel next?

711
00:48:21,231 --> 00:48:22,107
‪Here.

712
00:48:26,153 --> 00:48:29,072
‪-She was in Singapore until recently.
‪-Okay.

713
00:48:29,156 --> 00:48:30,574
‪The photos on her social media

714
00:48:30,657 --> 00:48:34,578
‪show the exhibition venues
‪and the art she handled.

715
00:48:35,829 --> 00:48:37,414
‪-This lady, though.
‪-Yeah?

716
00:48:37,497 --> 00:48:40,375
‪She must have a personal account
‪aside from this official one.

717
00:48:41,084 --> 00:48:41,960
‪You think so?

718
00:48:42,919 --> 00:48:44,129
‪Hold on.

719
00:48:45,464 --> 00:48:46,548
‪Here, open up.

720
00:48:46,632 --> 00:48:48,342
‪-Here? Or lower?
‪-Yes, there.

721
00:48:48,425 --> 00:48:50,052
‪-No, that side.
‪-This side?

722
00:48:50,135 --> 00:48:51,470
‪Your muscles are so tense.

723
00:48:51,553 --> 00:48:54,598
‪It's illegal to look up
‪one's credit card transactions.

724
00:48:54,681 --> 00:48:58,018
‪There's a limit to what I can find
‪on social media alone.

725
00:48:58,101 --> 00:49:01,730
‪Hyeong-min, that's exactly why
‪I came to you for help.

726
00:49:01,813 --> 00:49:03,190
‪On to your right shoulder.

727
00:49:03,815 --> 00:49:05,525
‪My gosh, this side is even worse.

728
00:49:13,533 --> 00:49:14,451
‪Mr. Ma.

729
00:49:17,204 --> 00:49:18,455
‪-Mr. Ma.
‪-Huh?

730
00:49:19,039 --> 00:49:20,248
‪Take a look at this.

731
00:49:21,083 --> 00:49:23,877
‪The same photo
‪keeps appearing on her feed.

732
00:49:24,586 --> 00:49:27,589
‪She seems to post it
‪whenever it comes to mind.

733
00:49:27,673 --> 00:49:28,715
‪Take a look.

734
00:49:31,259 --> 00:49:32,094
‪This place is…

735
00:49:34,429 --> 00:49:35,389
‪What time is it?

736
00:49:36,181 --> 00:49:38,100
‪I need to call that elder.

737
00:49:38,183 --> 00:49:39,267
‪Madam Pang?

738
00:49:39,351 --> 00:49:42,521
‪-Hyeong-min, I have a flight to catch.
‪-Okay.

739
00:49:42,604 --> 00:49:45,148
‪-Call me when you have something, okay?
‪-What?

740
00:49:45,232 --> 00:49:47,693
‪Thanks a lot.
‪Clean up after yourself. I love you.

741
00:49:47,776 --> 00:49:48,985
‪Mr. Ma.

742
00:49:50,445 --> 00:49:51,363
‪You punk.

743
00:49:55,033 --> 00:49:56,034
‪He got me again.

744
00:49:59,830 --> 00:50:00,664
‪Thank you.

745
00:50:03,792 --> 00:50:05,168
‪Hello, Mr. Bong.

746
00:50:05,794 --> 00:50:07,838
‪I just got it. All right.

747
00:50:08,422 --> 00:50:09,965
‪He's not there either?

748
00:50:11,466 --> 00:50:12,884
‪Okay then.

749
00:50:13,677 --> 00:50:16,221
‪I understand. Okay, bye.

750
00:50:17,222 --> 00:50:20,559
‪If he's not in Ms. Im's office,
‪he's not in the building.

751
00:50:20,642 --> 00:50:24,479
‪Where else could he be? His grandmother's?
‪No, she seemed clueless.

752
00:50:25,021 --> 00:50:27,274
‪He's never been late for work.

753
00:50:27,357 --> 00:50:29,818
‪It's eleven o'clock now, so where is he?

754
00:50:29,901 --> 00:50:32,028
‪Where on earth is he? Why--

755
00:50:33,113 --> 00:50:35,782
‪-Ma Gang-uk, this punk…
‪-Sir.

756
00:50:35,866 --> 00:50:37,117
‪He's over at…

757
00:50:37,200 --> 00:50:38,702
‪He went to Mr. Hwang's office.

758
00:50:38,785 --> 00:50:42,038
‪What are you on about?
‪That's where I'm coming from.

759
00:50:42,122 --> 00:50:45,542
‪-You see, Ma--
‪-Yes. He was there,

760
00:50:45,625 --> 00:50:48,378
‪then he went to the bathroom.
‪The men's, of course.

761
00:50:48,462 --> 00:50:49,796
‪He had a stomachache this morning.

762
00:50:49,880 --> 00:50:51,506
‪If it's urgent, I'll pass it to him

763
00:50:51,590 --> 00:50:52,883
‪-in the bath--
‪-What's with you?

764
00:50:53,508 --> 00:50:56,636
‪That punk called me at the crack of dawn

765
00:50:56,720 --> 00:50:58,722
‪and said he needed to take three days off.

766
00:50:59,222 --> 00:51:01,600
‪He just does whatever he pleases.

767
00:51:02,726 --> 00:51:03,769
‪Is something going on?

768
00:51:05,187 --> 00:51:07,105
‪-You don't know, do you?
‪-Well…

769
00:51:08,982 --> 00:51:10,317
‪I signed it, so process it.

770
00:51:11,193 --> 00:51:12,360
‪That troublemaker.

771
00:51:12,444 --> 00:51:13,653
‪LEAVE REQUEST: MA GANG-UK

772
00:51:15,447 --> 00:51:16,656
‪He took three days off.

773
00:51:16,740 --> 00:51:19,075
‪Why didn't he tell us? Where did he go?

774
00:51:19,159 --> 00:51:20,619
‪He went to Singapore.

775
00:51:20,702 --> 00:51:21,745
‪He actually went?

776
00:51:22,412 --> 00:51:25,373
‪After all that fuss, he actually went?

777
00:51:26,333 --> 00:51:28,293
‪What on earth is going on?

778
00:51:28,376 --> 00:51:30,712
‪Why didn't you tell me anything?

779
00:51:30,796 --> 00:51:33,799
‪I figured if I knew,
‪there was no way you didn't…

780
00:51:33,882 --> 00:51:35,926
‪I thought you'd know. I'm sorry.

781
00:51:36,968 --> 00:51:40,055
‪I stayed up working on something
‪with Mr. Ma,

782
00:51:40,138 --> 00:51:42,098
‪so I was a bit out of it this morning.

783
00:51:42,182 --> 00:51:45,560
‪You two stayed up last night without me?

784
00:51:46,895 --> 00:51:47,729
‪Yes.

785
00:51:47,813 --> 00:51:50,440
‪How come? Why wasn't I there?

786
00:51:50,524 --> 00:51:53,318
‪Why wasn't I included?
‪That's not fair. I'm hurt.

787
00:51:53,902 --> 00:51:55,237
‪Why would you feel hurt?

788
00:51:55,320 --> 00:51:56,363
‪You should be glad

789
00:51:56,446 --> 00:51:58,740
‪you didn't have to suffer
‪and stay up working.

790
00:51:58,824 --> 00:52:01,034
‪We only ate spicy rice cakes. That's it.

791
00:52:01,117 --> 00:52:02,118
‪Man, I'm tired.

792
00:52:04,079 --> 00:52:05,747
‪I saw traces of sushi.

793
00:52:05,831 --> 00:52:07,123
‪We had pizza too.

794
00:52:07,207 --> 00:52:08,917
‪I saw you had blood sausage too.

795
00:52:09,000 --> 00:52:11,419
‪-I swear I cleaned up.
‪-Darn you.

796
00:52:11,503 --> 00:52:13,380
‪-How could you?
‪-Okay. I'll treat you.

797
00:52:13,463 --> 00:52:15,340
‪I'll kill you if I catch you again.

798
00:52:27,727 --> 00:52:30,438
<i>‪Goodness, Yeo-ri is all you talk about.</i>

799
00:52:30,522 --> 00:52:32,232
‪Does she know you're like this?

800
00:52:32,315 --> 00:52:34,276
‪I might tell her on this trip.

801
00:52:49,583 --> 00:52:51,459
‪Yes, hello.

802
00:52:52,377 --> 00:52:53,920
‪I'd like to see you.

803
00:52:56,840 --> 00:52:57,799
‪Ma'am.

804
00:52:57,883 --> 00:53:00,969
‪A private investor called Danny Tan
‪invited Ms. Han.

805
00:53:01,052 --> 00:53:02,220
‪I just arranged a meeting with him.

806
00:53:02,804 --> 00:53:04,014
‪-Is that so?
‪-Yes.

807
00:53:04,097 --> 00:53:06,600
‪He wants to meet you
‪at the aquarium at 3 p.m.

808
00:53:07,434 --> 00:53:09,227
‪Okay. Good work.

809
00:53:17,652 --> 00:53:21,072
‪It's lovely here,
‪whatever time of year I visit.

810
00:53:21,781 --> 00:53:24,200
‪I love it here as well.

811
00:53:24,284 --> 00:53:26,661
‪The view is extra special today.

812
00:53:27,245 --> 00:53:30,707
‪And the tea tastes even better
‪with you here, Ms. Song.

813
00:53:31,499 --> 00:53:33,668
‪Take a nice walk around the grounds,

814
00:53:33,752 --> 00:53:36,046
‪and stay for dinner as well.

815
00:53:37,380 --> 00:53:40,800
‪Is Mr. Ma doing well?

816
00:53:40,884 --> 00:53:43,094
‪I only saw him from afar,

817
00:53:43,178 --> 00:53:44,763
‪but he seemed to be doing well.

818
00:53:46,181 --> 00:53:48,099
‪He's so busy with work.

819
00:53:48,183 --> 00:53:50,518
‪I got a call from him
‪the day after the ceremony

820
00:53:50,602 --> 00:53:52,312
‪and nothing since.

821
00:53:54,814 --> 00:53:57,817
‪Actually, I asked to see you because…

822
00:53:58,485 --> 00:54:01,071
‪Yes, of course. I'm listening.

823
00:54:02,530 --> 00:54:03,448
‪Well…

824
00:54:04,866 --> 00:54:07,953
‪Could you arrange for me
‪to meet Mr. Ma over a meal?

825
00:54:08,912 --> 00:54:11,790
‪You can introduce me
‪as a close acquaintance.

826
00:54:11,873 --> 00:54:14,709
‪Yes, of course. I can do that.

827
00:54:14,793 --> 00:54:17,837
‪I'll arrange something,
‪then call you right away.

828
00:54:18,421 --> 00:54:19,255
‪By the way,

829
00:54:19,339 --> 00:54:23,218
‪you said you're well-acquainted
‪with his fiancée's grandmother.

830
00:54:23,301 --> 00:54:27,055
‪We're in the same field,
‪as you already know.

831
00:54:27,138 --> 00:54:30,433
‪Yeo-ri and Ji-hwan were friends
‪since they were young,

832
00:54:30,517 --> 00:54:32,352
‪and they went to the same school too.

833
00:54:32,936 --> 00:54:34,479
‪Oh, they were friends?

834
00:54:37,357 --> 00:54:38,733
‪They're not the same age, are they?

835
00:54:39,275 --> 00:54:41,569
‪Ji-hwan was born
‪in the year of the monkey,

836
00:54:41,653 --> 00:54:43,446
‪and Yeo-ri was born
‪in the year of the goat.

837
00:54:44,614 --> 00:54:45,782
‪That can't be.

838
00:54:46,658 --> 00:54:49,119
‪Yeo-ri and Ji-hwan are the same age.

839
00:55:15,770 --> 00:55:16,730
‪Whose is this?

840
00:55:19,024 --> 00:55:20,150
‪MAY 8, 1991, 18:00
‪FEMALE, YEAR OF THE GOAT

841
00:55:22,569 --> 00:55:23,403
‪Could it be…

842
00:55:23,486 --> 00:55:25,363
‪No need for excuses.

843
00:55:27,198 --> 00:55:28,283
‪That date and time of birth.

844
00:55:29,117 --> 00:55:31,119
‪Who does it really belong to?

845
00:55:31,828 --> 00:55:33,830
‪Oh, right. This…

846
00:55:33,913 --> 00:55:36,291
‪This is my wife's date of birth.

847
00:55:36,374 --> 00:55:37,751
‪You see…

848
00:55:37,834 --> 00:55:39,836
‪Okay. I'm really sorry.

849
00:55:41,504 --> 00:55:43,256
‪What am I to do with that punk?

850
00:55:43,757 --> 00:55:45,467
‪Perhaps I could explain…

851
00:55:45,550 --> 00:55:47,927
‪Make an excuse?
‪I wouldn't call it an excuse.

852
00:55:48,011 --> 00:55:50,805
‪Gang-uk was really stressed out over this,

853
00:55:50,889 --> 00:55:52,974
‪and he kept letting out deep sighs.

854
00:55:53,058 --> 00:55:55,060
‪Since I'm older than him,
‪I wanted to help him out.

855
00:55:55,143 --> 00:55:57,437
‪For their love, their true love…

856
00:55:57,520 --> 00:55:58,563
‪Enough.

857
00:55:59,856 --> 00:56:00,857
‪So,

858
00:56:02,358 --> 00:56:05,111
‪where is Gang-uk right now?

859
00:57:29,654 --> 00:57:30,488
‪Hello?

860
00:57:30,572 --> 00:57:32,198
<i>‪Ma'am, it's about Danny Tan.</i>

861
00:57:32,282 --> 00:57:35,326
<i>‪He called to say he had to attend</i>
<i>‪another urgent meeting.</i>

862
00:57:36,369 --> 00:57:37,454
<i>‪What should I do?</i>

863
00:57:54,095 --> 00:57:55,763
‪All right. Bye.

864
00:58:24,250 --> 00:58:25,084
‪Gang-uk.

865
00:59:41,035 --> 00:59:43,454
‪SPOOKY IN LOVE

866
00:59:44,455 --> 00:59:45,665
‪I missed you so much, Yeo-ri.

867
00:59:47,333 --> 00:59:49,711
<i>‪I'm glad you're here with me.</i>

868
00:59:49,794 --> 00:59:50,962
‪-Cheers.
‪-Cheers.

869
00:59:52,046 --> 00:59:54,340
‪Want to come in for a cup of tea?

870
00:59:54,924 --> 00:59:57,885
‪How can I be sure that my 3%
‪will be enough for you to win?

871
00:59:57,969 --> 00:59:59,178
‪You're desperate.

872
00:59:59,804 --> 01:00:01,347
‪Don't you want to protect it?

873
01:00:01,431 --> 01:00:04,350
‪We will now begin the extraordinary
‪general meeting of shareholders

874
01:00:04,434 --> 01:00:07,103
<i>‪regarding the motion for removal</i>
<i>‪of Reina Hotel's CEO, Cheon Yeo-ri.</i>

875
01:00:07,186 --> 01:00:09,856
<i>‪Then Cheon Yeo-ri will</i>
<i>‪no longer have a hold on Reina.</i>

876
01:00:09,939 --> 01:00:11,232
‪Ma Gang-uk, was it?

877
01:00:11,316 --> 01:00:12,442
‪Is he giving you trouble?

878
01:00:14,110 --> 01:00:15,236
‪What's going on here?

879
01:00:15,320 --> 01:00:17,822
‪You've been reassigned
‪to an overseas training program.

880
01:00:17,905 --> 01:00:18,906
‪Gang-uk is

881
01:00:19,657 --> 01:00:21,034
<i>‪going abroad?</i>

882
01:00:21,117 --> 01:00:24,704
‪Subtitle translation by: Jennifer Jean Lim
